{number: 14}
{title: How Great Thou Art}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [Bb] Lord, my God! When I in [Eb] awesome wonder
Con-[Bb] sider all the [F] worlds Thy hands have [Bb] made,
I [Bb] see the stars, I hear the [Eb] rolling thunder,
Thy [Bb] power through-[F] out the universe dis-[Bb] played.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Then sings my [Bb] soul, my [Eb] Savior God, to [Bb] Thee:
How great Thou [Cm] art, [F7] how great Thou [Bb] art! [F]
Then sings my [Bb] soul, my [Eb] Savior God, to [Bb] Thee:
How great Thou [Cm] art, [F7] how great Thou [Bb] art!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [Bb] through the woods and forest [Eb] glades I wander,
And [Bb] hear the birds sing [F] sweetly in the [Bb] trees;
When [Bb] I look down from lofty [Eb] mountain grandeur,
And [Bb] hear the brook and [F] feel the gentle [Bb] breeze.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [Bb] when I think that God, His [Eb] Son not sparing,
Sent [Bb] Him to die, I [F] scarce can take it [Bb] in;
That [Bb] on the cross, my burden [Eb] gladly bearing,
He [Bb] bled and died to [F] take away my [Bb] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [Bb] Christ shall come, with shout of [Eb] acclamation,
And [Bb] take me home, what [F] joy shall fill my [Bb] heart!
Then [Bb] I shall bow in humble [Eb] adoration,
And [Bb] there proclaim, my [F] God, how great Thou [Bb] art!
{end_of_verse}
